post.description:
Create or update multiple DataTables from a Frictionless Data Package (UPSERT).

This endpoint is idempotent - it can be called multiple times with the same schema.
- If table doesn't exist: Creates new DataTable with auto-materialization
- If table exists: Updates schema using incremental migrations (ADD/DROP/ALTER columns)

Accepts a Data Package with multiple table resources. Defaults to 'flat_table'
provider type unless specified in each resource.

Uses Alembic Operations API with topological sorting to handle foreign key
dependencies intelligently. Tables are created/updated in dependency order.

POST /api/apps/{app_slug}/datatables/create_schema/
POST /api/apps/{app_slug}/datatables/create_schema/?materialize=true

Request Body (Frictionless Data Package format):
{
    "name": "my_package",
    "title": "My Package",
    "description": "Package description",
    "resources": [
        {
            "name": "users",
            "schema": {
                "fields": [
                    {"name": "id", "type": "integer"},
                    {"name": "name", "type": "string"}
                ],
                "primaryKey": ["id"]
            },
            "provider_type": "flat_table"  # Optional, defaults to flat_table
        },
        {
            "name": "posts",
            "schema": {
                "fields": [
                    {"name": "id", "type": "integer"},
                    {"name": "user_id", "type": "integer"},
                    {"name": "content", "type": "string"}
                ],
                "primaryKey": ["id"],
                "foreignKeys": [
                    {
                        "fields": ["user_id"],
                        "reference": {
                            "resource": "users",
                            "fields": ["id"]
                        }
                    }
                ]
            }
        }
    ]
}

Response:
{
    "created_count": 1,
    "updated_count": 1,
    "error_count": 0,
    "created_tables": [
        {
            "id": 1,
            "name": "users",
            "physical_table_name": "myapp_users",
            "provider_type": "flat_table",
            "is_materialized": true,
            "field_count": 2
        }
    ],
    "updated_tables": [
        {
            "id": 2,
            "name": "posts",
            "physical_table_name": "myapp_posts",
            "provider_type": "flat_table",
            "is_materialized": true,
            "field_count": 3
        }
    ],
    "errors": []
}

Note: Tables are processed in dependency order, so parent tables are always
created/updated before child tables with foreign keys.

delete.description:
Delete multiple edges by IDs.

**Request Body**:
```json
{
  "edge_ids": [1, 2, 3, 4, 5]
}
```

**Response**:
```json
{
  "status": "success",
  "message": "Successfully deleted 5 record(s)",
  "data": {"deleted_count": 5}
}
```

SuccessDataResponse.description:
Standardized data response format for Django Ninja APIs.

Handles both single items and lists. Use optional `total` for paginated lists.

Example (single item):
    {
        "status": "success",
        "message": "Resource retrieved successfully",
        "data": {...}
    }

Example (list with total):
    {
        "status": "success",
        "message": "Data retrieved successfully",
        "data": [...],
        "total": 100
    }
